The Betrayer#Castle Route and Door Keys	29	{"kind":"quest","title":"The Betrayer","wikiPath":"/The_Betrayer","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Lady Sileniu Everling","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[],"card":{"title":"The Betrayer","lines":["Minimum Level: ?","Classes: ALL","Related Zones: Nektropos Castle","Related NPCs: Lady Sileniu Everling, Plimptos, Alexa`s Handmaiden, Alexa Everling, Lord Rikantus Everling"]},"links":["Nektropos Castle","Lady Sileniu Everling","Plimptos","Alexa`s Handmaiden","Alexa Everling","Lord Rikantus Everling","Blood's Unity","Jenni Everling","Melanie Everling","Crysta Everling","Shelia Everling","Elise Everling","Deirdre Everling","Nektropos Great Room Key","The Tragic Tale of House Everling","The Tragic Tale of House Everling#Castle Access and Library Key","Nektropos Private Chamber Key","Guard Captain Ga`Vin","The Juggernaught","Nektropos Basement Key","The Tragic Tale of House Everling#Quest Dialogue and Completion","Host of Nektropos","Fractured Malice"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Lady Sileniu Everling","text":"[He] must pay! He must pay for what he did to my children! He must pay for what he did to my family! I thought leaving this world would bring me peace but there is only pain."},{"npc":"Lady Sileniu Everling","text":"Plimptos! And his other damnable eunuchs. May they suffer for all time in the plane of torment. But Plimptos still walks this earth... while my daughters lie slain. Please [swear] to me that you will right this injustice and allow me to rest in peace."},{"npc":"Lady Sileniu Everling","text":"Oh thank you Soandso. You are a walking blessing for our family. Now go! He should be locked away still. Go and find him and not allow him to draw another breath in this world."},{"npc":"Plimptos","text":"Another has come to administer my torture session. Stangely though, I do not know you. Are you from outside the castle? Then please listen to my tale and help me atone for my regrettable [crimes]."},{"npc":"Plimptos","text":"I have done many things in my life but none so reprehensible as this. It was anger and maybe madness that drove me, but I killed them all. All the sisters I swore to care for. I killed them and cut them into tiny pieces as small as the sword would cut them. It was almost like a dream. The blood flowing as I slashed and hacked my way room from room making sure there was no way Rikantus would ever be able to lay his eyes on his cherished children ever again. I paid for it. I have died more times than I have ever killed. Each time being [brought back] from the safety of death only to relive torture and pain again."},{"npc":"Plimptos","text":"Yes, a curse of some kind as punishment for my deeds has me resurrected every time. Maybe one-hundred times or a thousand at this point I do not know anymore. There is one way that may end this cycle of suffering. Please, take this sword hilt and find the spirits of the seven sisters. Recreate my evil deeds in a final act and put them to rest so that I may then finally be able to rest myself."},{"npc":"Alexa`s Handmaiden","text":"I apologize, but Alexa is not here right now. Perhaps you should see if she is visiting one of her sisters in their towers?"},{"npc":"Alexa`s Handmaiden","text":"Alexa was not with her sisters? You should try in the great room, then. Take this key and see if you can find her there."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-10-28T06:54:25.987Z","outOfEra":false}
